"type": "organizational"}, "role": {"id": "hostinginstitution", "title": {"de": "Bereitstellende Institution", "en": "Hosting institution"}}}, {"person_or_org": {"name": "Pular Consulting", "type": "organizational"}, "role": {"id": "sponsor", "title": {"de": "Sponsor", "en": "Sponsor"}}}], "creators": [{"affiliations": [{"name": "Empiria Lab"}, {"id": "03gtdcg60", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "03gtdcg60", "scheme": "ror"}, {"identifier": "grid.412193.c", "scheme": "grid"}, {"identifier": "0000 0001 2150 3115", "scheme": "isni"}], "name": "Universidad Diego Portales"}, {"id": "027bh9e22", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "027bh9e22", "scheme": "ror"}, {"identifier": "grid.5132.5", "scheme": "grid"}, {"identifier": "0000 0001 2312 1970", "scheme": "isni"}], "name": "Leiden University"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Gonz\u00e1lez-Bustamante", "given_name": "Basti\u00e1n", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0003-1510-6820", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Gonz\u00e1lez-Bustamante, Basti\u00e1n", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "Empiria Lab"}, {"id": "03gtdcg60", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "03gtdcg60", "scheme": "ror"}, {"identifier": "grid.412193.c", "scheme": "grid"}, {"identifier": "0000 0001 2150 3115", "scheme": "isni"}], "name": "Universidad Diego Portales"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Verelst", "given_name": "Nando", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0002-0957-767X", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Verelst, Nando", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [{"name": "Empiria Lab"}, {"id": "027bh9e22", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "027bh9e22", "scheme": "ror"}, {"identifier": "grid.5132.5", "scheme": "grid"}, {"identifier": "0000 0001 2312 1970", "scheme": "isni"}], "name": "Leiden University"}], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Cisternas", "given_name": "Carla", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0001-7948-6194", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Cisternas, Carla", "type": "personal"}}], "description": "\u003cp\u003eLarge Language Models (LLMs) offer promising avenues for methodological and applied innovations in survey research by using synthetic respondents to emulate human answers and behaviour, potentially mitigating measurement and representation errors. However, the extent to which LLMs recover aggregate item distributions remains uncertain and downstream applications risk reproducing social stereotypes and biases inherited from training data. We evaluate the reliability of LLM-generated synthetic survey responses against ground-truth human responses from a Chilean public opinion probabilistic survey. Specifically, we benchmark 128 prompt-model-question triplets, generating 189,696 synthetic profiles, and pool performance metrics (i.e., accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score) in a meta-analysis across 128 question-subsample pairs to test for biases along key sociodemographic dimensions. The evaluation spans OpenAI\u0026rsquo;s GPT family and o-series reasoning models, as well as Llama and Qwen checkpoints. Three results stand out. First, synthetic responses achieve excellent performance on trust items (F1-score and accuracy \u0026gt; 0.90). Second, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini and Llama 4 Maverick perform comparably on this task. Third, synthetic-human alignment is highest among respondents aged 45-59. Overall, LLM-based synthetic samples approximate responses from a probabilistic sample, though with substantial item-level heterogeneity. Capturing the full nuance of public opinion remains challenging and requires careful calibration and additional distributional tests to ensure algorithmic fidelity and reduce errors.\u003c/p\u003e", "languages": [{"id": "eng", "title": {"en": "English"}}], "publication_date": "2025-09-18", "publisher": "Zenodo", "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2509.09871", "relation_type": {"id": "isnewversionof", "title": {"de": "Ist eine neue Version von", "en": "Is new version of"}}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-preprint", "title": {"de": "Preprint", "en": "Preprint"}}, "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"id": "publication-workingpaper", "title": {"de": "Arbeitspapier", "en": "Working paper"}}, "rights": [{"description": {"en": "The Creative Commons Attribution license allows re-distribution and re-use of a licensed work on the condition that the creator is appropriately credited."}, "icon": "cc-by-icon", "id": "cc-by-4.0", "props": {"scheme": "spdx", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"}, "title": {"en": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}}], "title": "Emulating Public Opinion: A Proof-of-Concept of AI-Generated Synthetic Survey Responses for the Chilean Case"}, "parent": {"access": {"owned_by": {"user": "265229"}, "settings": {"accept_conditions_text": null, "allow_guest_requests": false, "allow_user_requests": false, "secret_link_expiration": 0}}, "communities": {"default": "c1162cda-e961-48b4-a0f4-bfa7641e45d7", "entries": [{"access": {"member_policy": "open", "members_visibility": "public", "record_submission_policy": "open", "review_policy": "closed", "visibility": "public"}, "children": {"allow": false}, "created": "2025-09-08T10:47:08.106925+00:00", "custom_fields": {"subjects": [{"id": "mesh:D000077488"}, {"id": "mesh:D012942"}, {"id": "euroscivoc:297"}]}, "deletion_status": {"is_deleted": false, "status": "P"}, "id": "c1162cda-e961-48b4-a0f4-bfa7641e45d7", "links": {}, "metadata": {"curation_policy": "\u003cp\u003eLab-sponsored projects, data sets and working papers. If you have any questions, please send an email to repository@empirialab.cl.\u003c/p\u003e", "description": "We are a team specialised in data science and artificial intelligence, delivering technological solutions and data analysis to public and private sector clients.", "page": "\u003cp\u003eEmpiria Lab is a team that offers innovative technological solutions for organisations seeking to make a positive impact on the world.\u0026nbsp;Our team is made up of professionals with extensive experience in management, social research, data science, and artificial intelligence.\u003c/p\u003e", "title": "Empiria Lab", "type": {"id": "organization"}, "website": "https://empirialab.cl"}, "revision_id": 8, "slug": "empirialab", "updated": "2025-09-19T18:34:04.837721+00:00"}], "ids": ["c1162cda-e961-48b4-a0f4-bfa7641e45d7"]}, "id": "17077751", "pids": {"doi": {"client": "datacite", "identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.17077751", "provider": "datacite"}}}, "pids": {"doi": {"client": "datacite", "identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.17077752", "provider": "datacite"}, "oai": {"identifier": "oai:zenodo.org:17077752", "provider": "oai"}}, "revision_id": 10, "stats": {"all_versions": {"data_volume": 513025169.0, "downloads": 653, "unique_downloads": 489, "unique_views": 822, "views": 966}, "this_version": {"data_volume": 325251234.0, "downloads": 414, "unique_downloads": 299, "unique_views": 428, "views": 532}}, "status": "published", "swh": {}, "ui": {"access_status": {"description_l10n": "The record and files are publicly accessible.", "embargo_date_l10n": null, "icon": "unlock", "id": "open", "message_class": "", "title_l10n": "Open"}, "contributors": {"affiliations": [], "contributors": [{"person_or_org": {"name": "Empiria Lab", "type": "organizational"}, "role": {"id": "hostinginstitution", "title": "Hosting institution"}}, {"person_or_org": {"name": "Pular Consulting", "type": "organizational"}, "role": {"id": "sponsor", "title": "Sponsor"}}]}, "created_date_l10n_long": "September 18, 2025", "creators": {"affiliations": [[1, "Empiria Lab", null], [2, "Universidad Diego Portales", "03gtdcg60"], [3, "Leiden University", "027bh9e22"]], "creators": [{"affiliations": [[1, "Empiria Lab"], [2, "Universidad Diego Portales"], [3, "Leiden University"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Gonz\u00e1lez-Bustamante", "given_name": "Basti\u00e1n", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0003-1510-6820", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Gonz\u00e1lez-Bustamante, Basti\u00e1n", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "Empiria Lab"], [2, "Universidad Diego Portales"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Verelst", "given_name": "Nando", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0002-0957-767X", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Verelst, Nando", "type": "personal"}}, {"affiliations": [[1, "Empiria Lab"], [3, "Leiden University"]], "person_or_org": {"family_name": "Cisternas", "given_name": "Carla", "identifiers": [{"identifier": "0000-0001-7948-6194", "scheme": "orcid"}], "name": "Cisternas, Carla", "type": "personal"}}]}, "custom_fields": {"journal:journal": {"issn": "3087-2553", "issue": "1", "title": "Empiria Lab Method Series"}}, "description_stripped": "Large Language Models (LLMs) offer promising avenues for methodological and applied innovations in survey research by using synthetic respondents to emulate human answers and behaviour, potentially mitigating measurement and representation errors. However, the extent to which LLMs recover aggregate item distributions remains uncertain and downstream applications risk reproducing social stereotypes and biases inherited from training data. We evaluate the reliability of LLM-generated synthetic survey responses against ground-truth human responses from a Chilean public opinion probabilistic survey. Specifically, we benchmark 128 prompt-model-question triplets, generating 189,696 synthetic profiles, and pool performance metrics (i.e., accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score) in a meta-analysis across 128 question-subsample pairs to test for biases along key sociodemographic dimensions. The evaluation spans OpenAI\u2019s GPT family and o-series reasoning models, as well as Llama and Qwen checkpoints. Three results stand out. First, synthetic responses achieve excellent performance on trust items (F1-score and accuracy \u003e 0.90). Second, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini and Llama 4 Maverick perform comparably on this task. Third, synthetic-human alignment is highest among respondents aged 45-59. Overall, LLM-based synthetic samples approximate responses from a probabilistic sample, though with substantial item-level heterogeneity. Capturing the full nuance of public opinion remains challenging and requires careful calibration and additional distributional tests to ensure algorithmic fidelity and reduce errors.", "is_draft": false, "languages": [{"id": "eng", "title_l10n": "English"}], "publication_date_l10n_long": "September 18, 2025", "publication_date_l10n_medium": "Sep 18, 2025", "publishing_information": {"journal": "Empiria Lab Method Series, 1, ISSN: 3087-2553, 2025."}, "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2509.09871", "relation_type": {"id": "isnewversionof", "title_l10n": "Is new version of"}, "resource_type": {"id": "publication-preprint", "title_l10n": "Preprint"}, "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"id": "publication-workingpaper", "title_l10n": "Working paper"}, "rights": [{"description_l10n": "The Creative Commons Attribution license allows re-distribution and re-use of a licensed work on the condition that the creator is appropriately credited.", "icon": "cc-by-icon", "id": "cc-by-4.0", "props": {"scheme": "spdx", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"}, "title_l10n": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}], "updated_date_l10n_long": "October 14, 2025", "version": "v1"}, "updated": "2025-10-14T17:49:57.735476+00:00", "versions": {"index": 1, "is_latest": false}}'
